# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_extractor_elixir.py" "ELIXIR GATE: PASS" "Elixir extractor (defmodule/def/defp/defmacro nodes + calls edges)" "Elixir .ex/.exs files now mint def-kind nodes for functions and class-kind nodes for modules, with content-free line spans and cross-module calls edges." "THE GAP FIXED: .ex/.exs were already in _SOURCE_EXT (file nodes existed) but tree_sitter_elixir was absent from _ts_languages() so the grammar was never loaded and 0 structural edges were produced. Elixir's grammar does NOT use distinct node types for definitions: defmodule/def/defp/defmacro/defmacrop are ALL call nodes distinguished only by the first-child identifier text -- _GENERIC_SPEC (which dispatches on node TYPE) cannot handle this. A bespoke extract_file_elixir() walker was added to _cg_languages.py (analogous to extract_file_svelte) and registered in _ts_languages(). Routing was added in code_graph_extract.py before the generic spec path. MEASURED on the Phoenix framework repo (phoenixframework/phoenix): BEFORE 0 def+class nodes from 176 .ex/.exs files; AFTER 1632 def+class nodes (334 module/class nodes + 1298 function/macro def nodes) from the same 176 files, with real names confirmed (Phoenix.MixProject, Phoenix.Router, Phoenix.Channel, ActionController, etc.) and correct line spans. WHAT THIS GATE PROVES (hermetic, no DB, no Postgres, no network): (1) defmodule MyApp.Accounts mints a class-kind node; (2) def get_user mints a def-kind node; (3) defp validate mints a def-kind node (private functions are first-class symbols); (4) defmacro my_macro mints a def-kind node; (5) a second module in the same file mints its own class node; (6) Module.function() dot-calls emit calls edges; (7) empty .ex file does not crash; (8) malformed .ex file does not crash; (9) content-free -- a secret literal in a .ex file does not appear in the graph; (10) line spans (start_line/end_line) are present on def/class nodes." 20
